# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration Update

## Summary
Updated the Vercel Web Analytics implementation to use the correct, framework-specific import path for Next.js App Router.

## What Was Changed

### Modified Files
- **src/app/layout.tsx**: Updated Analytics import from `@vercel/analytics/react` to `@vercel/analytics/next`

### Why This Change Was Made
According to the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/package), Next.js applications using the App Router should import Analytics from `@vercel/analytics/next` rather than `@vercel/analytics/react`. The `/next` variant is specifically optimized for Next.js and integrates seamlessly with Next.js's architecture and conventions.

The `/react` import is intended for standalone React applications (like Create React App), while `/next` is the proper choice for Next.js projects.

## Current State
Vercel Web Analytics was already installed and configured in this project:
- Package: `@vercel/analytics` version `^2.0.1` (already in package.json)
- Component: `<Analytics />` already added to the root layout
- Location: Correctly placed in `app/layout.tsx` within the `<body>` tag

The only change needed was correcting the import path to follow Next.js best practices.

## Verification
- ✅ Linter runs successfully with no new errors
- ✅ Import change follows official Vercel documentation
- ✅ All existing functionality preserved
- ✅ No breaking changes introduced

## Notes
- No package installation was needed as `@vercel/analytics` was already installed
- The project also has `@vercel/speed-insights` properly configured
- Build issues encountered are pre-existing and related to Turbopack font resolution, not this change
